1
00:00:14,525 --> 00:00:20,566
You two will be seconded to Zaō Kōsoku Electric Railway for one week.

2
00:00:21,666 --> 00:00:22,958
Yes.

3
00:00:22,958 --> 00:00:25,333
A staff exchange?

4
00:00:25,708 --> 00:00:28,666
That's right. This year, it's a joint program with the Transport Command division too.

5
00:00:29,208 --> 00:00:30,720
Nice, Yamagata!

6
00:00:31,126 --> 00:00:33,475
Zaoden, so jealous!

7
00:00:33,499 --> 00:00:38,487
It's the line connecting Kaminoyama-Onsen Station, Yamagata Station, and Zao-Onsen Station!

8
00:00:38,511 --> 00:00:43,750
Plus, they have special trains that run on the dual-gauge single-track parallel sections of the Ou Main Line and Senzan Line!

9
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:45,166
Yeah, yeah.

10
00:00:45,166 --> 00:00:47,901
Buy me platform tickets -- for every station!

11
00:00:47,926 --> 00:00:48,934
No.

12
00:00:48,988 --> 00:00:50,750
Aww!

13
00:00:50,777 --> 00:00:53,193
Bring back souvenirs for us too, okay?

14
00:00:53,583 --> 00:00:55,375
Earl Grey with safflower, please.

15
00:00:56,208 --> 00:01:00,374
And so, we headed off to Yamagata.

16
00:01:09,291 --> 00:01:11,625
We made it to Zao!

17
00:01:11,625 --> 00:01:12,750
Hot springs!

18
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:14,166
Skiing!

19
00:01:14,166 --> 00:01:15,916
Imoni stew party!

20
00:01:15,916 --> 00:01:16,958
We're here to work.

21
00:01:20,791 --> 00:01:25,208
So, everyone -- these folks have come to us from Kyoki Railway.

22
00:01:26,208 --> 00:01:28,500
Pleased to meet you!

23
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:30,458
We'll give it our apple -- I mean, our all!

24
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,875
Uh... "apple"? Is that a local dialect thing?

25
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:40,334
Now then, Hosono-san and Agaho-san -- our new hire will show you around.

26
00:01:40,534 --> 00:01:41,541
Okay.

27
00:01:41,541 --> 00:01:44,367
Zeze-san and Konosu-san, please come this way...

28
00:01:44,565 --> 00:01:45,654
Sure.

29
00:01:49,064 --> 00:01:50,074
I'm Mega!

30
00:01:50,099 --> 00:01:51,166
Hello.

31
00:01:51,166 --> 00:01:53,541
Looking forward to working with you this week!

32
00:01:53,541 --> 00:01:54,916
But I refuse.

33
00:01:54,916 --> 00:01:56,875
Whyyy?!

34
00:01:56,875 --> 00:02:01,046
I'm swamped arranging the crowdfunding reward perks right now.

35
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:06,458
This year's Hot Spring Safflower Train was funded by contributions from lots of supporters.

36
00:02:06,791 --> 00:02:09,291
Wait -- a train?

37
00:02:09,291 --> 00:02:10,541
Through crowdfunding?

38
00:02:10,541 --> 00:02:13,813
Yes. Our railway basically only carries tourists,

39
00:02:13,837 --> 00:02:16,661
so with ridership plummeting, we're in serious trouble.

40
00:02:16,685 --> 00:02:20,583
At this point, crowdfunding is pretty much our main revenue stream.

41
00:02:20,583 --> 00:02:21,790
Oh my...

42
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:25,661
Shipping out the thank-you merchandise to backers is our top priority mission.

43
00:02:25,685 --> 00:02:30,541
That's why I'm so busy!

44
00:02:30,541 --> 00:02:33,928
Hello, Zaō Kōsoku Electric Railway.

45
00:02:33,952 --> 00:02:41,875
What...? The delivery? ...I see.

46
00:02:41,875 --> 00:02:43,750
It's over.

47
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:46,750
...We're done for.

48
00:02:46,783 --> 00:02:48,289
Huh, what happened?

49
00:02:48,375 --> 00:02:52,695
The manufacturer for the reward perks went bankrupt. They can't deliver anymore.

50
00:02:52,719 --> 00:02:57,333
It's a specialty product, so even if we find a new supplier now, it won't be in time.

51
00:02:57,333 --> 00:03:01,486
Then we need to notify the backers about the delay right away!

52
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:05,375
Leave it to me! Writing apology letters is the one thing I'm good at!

53
00:03:05,375 --> 00:03:08,500
Uhh...

54
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:13,541
One hour later...

55
00:03:13,541 --> 00:03:15,250
Done!

56
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:16,875
Got the OK from the president!

57
00:03:17,125 --> 00:03:18,289
Alright, let's send the email!

58
00:03:18,416 --> 00:03:19,541
Right!

59
00:03:19,541 --> 00:03:22,625
STOP!

60
00:03:22,625 --> 00:03:28,625
Don't send it. Step away from the computer with your hands up.

61
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,500
Huh? What?

62
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:35,875
You've put every single customer's email address in the To field.

63
00:03:35,875 --> 00:03:37,666
So?

64
00:03:37,666 --> 00:03:43,500
Email addresses in the To or CC fields are visible to every recipient!

65
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:45,500
That would be a personal information leak?!

66
00:03:45,656 --> 00:03:49,431
Yes. When sending a mass email,

67
00:03:49,455 --> 00:03:53,834
put the customers' email addresses in the BCC field.

68
00:03:54,117 --> 00:03:57,163
B-C-C.

69
00:03:57,187 --> 00:04:02,416
That way, the recipients' addresses won't be visible to the others.

70
00:04:02,416 --> 00:04:04,083
I had no idea!

71
00:04:04,083 --> 00:04:09,444
Actually, for this case, let's use the crowdfunding site's messaging feature instead of email.

72
00:04:09,468 --> 00:04:11,041
That'll be more reliable.

73
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:17,500
Okay.

74
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:20,375
...Sending now.

75
00:04:20,375 --> 00:04:23,866
We're so sorry... So very sorry...

76
00:04:27,541 --> 00:04:30,916
Well, here it comes...

77
00:04:30,916 --> 00:04:32,583
Should I answer it?

78
00:04:32,583 --> 00:04:36,666
No, I will. I'm prepared for the worst.

79
00:04:36,666 --> 00:04:39,916
Hello, Zaō Kōsoku Electric Railway.

80
00:04:39,916 --> 00:04:43,958
I read the message.

81
00:04:43,958 --> 00:04:51,166
I'll wait for the finished product even if it's late! Keep at it! I'm rooting for you!

82
00:04:51,166 --> 00:04:53,333
I'm a fan. Hang in there!

83
00:04:53,666 --> 00:04:55,333
I-It's only this once, okay?!

84
00:04:55,333 --> 00:04:59,125
Don't let the hard times get you down, y'hear?

85
00:04:59,125 --> 00:05:02,500
...Thank you so much! Thank you!

86
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:05,917
And so, they were flooded with calls of encouragement.

87
00:05:05,941 --> 00:05:09,707
That just shows how much their customers love them.

88
00:05:09,731 --> 00:05:14,083
I'm a little jealous, honestly.

89
00:05:14,083 --> 00:05:16,166
Hello, Zaō Kōsoku Electric Railway.

90
00:05:16,625 --> 00:05:23,416
I know a factory that can make those goods! I'll put you in touch! Oh, and I'd like to buy platform tickets -- for every station!

91
00:05:23,416 --> 00:05:24,708
R-Really?!

92
00:05:24,708 --> 00:05:29,833
Hmm, that voice just now sounded familiar somehow...

93
00:05:29,833 --> 00:05:34,708
With all that commotion, the week flew by in no time--

94
00:05:34,708 --> 00:05:37,333
Thank you so, so much!

95
00:05:37,333 --> 00:05:39,750
Glad it looks like things will work out.

96
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:40,916
Truly.

97
00:05:40,916 --> 00:05:45,125
By the way, what exactly is the Hot Spring Safflower Train?

98
00:05:45,125 --> 00:05:52,458
It's a special train that departs from our Zao-Onsen Station, runs via the national railway, and goes all the way to Takase Station -- famous for its safflower fields.

99
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:59,000
The safflower fields stretching out as far as you can see, all dyed in orange -- they're beautiful.

100
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,458
Huh, "crimson" flower but they're orange! I wanna see that!

101
00:06:03,541 --> 00:06:07,250
I'm sorry, the season's already over...

102
00:06:07,250 --> 00:06:08,916
Oh, really...

103
00:06:08,916 --> 00:06:13,500
But the Cosmos Berg at Mt. Omoshiroyama is about to be in full bloom!

104
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:16,958
Mt. Omoshiroyama? Sounds like a fun place!

105
00:06:17,625 --> 00:06:22,125
As a thank-you for this week, I'll take everyone there!

106
00:06:22,125 --> 00:06:26,250
Really? Are you sure?!

107
00:06:26,783 --> 00:06:32,283
Next stop, Omoshiroyama-Kogen. Next stop, Omoshiroyama-Kogen.

108
00:06:38,208 --> 00:06:40,708
Wow!

109
00:06:40,708 --> 00:06:43,166
Yellow cosmos flowers everywhere!

110
00:06:43,166 --> 00:06:44,916
Beautiful!

111
00:06:44,916 --> 00:06:52,750
What a lovely place. I'd like to come back for the safflowers next time. I wonder if they look something like this...

112
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:57,708
Come to think of it, safflowers and cosmos are both in the Asteraceae family, right?

113
00:06:58,250 --> 00:07:04,500
Why would you "aster" me that?

114
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:11,416
Oh! This is actually a ski resort! Too bad we can't ski right now.

115
00:07:11,791 --> 00:07:14,500
Don't worry. You can still do some sliding here.

116
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,208
Really?!

117
00:07:16,875 --> 00:07:19,750
At Cosmos Berg, even the jokes fall flat-berg!

118
00:07:19,750 --> 00:07:22,541
Ugh...

119
00:07:22,541 --> 00:07:28,500
Hot springs... I just want to go to the hot springs...

120
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:34,833
Well, I guess Mt. Omoshiroyama certainly has some... interesting characters!

121
00:08:35,383 --> 00:08:36,983
Revival!!

122
00:08:48,039 --> 00:08:52,094
I've always liked you. It's only ever been you.

123
00:08:52,119 --> 00:08:53,183
Huh...?

124
00:08:53,208 --> 00:08:55,828
So... would you go out with me?

125
00:09:01,284 --> 00:09:04,895
...You win. I admit total defeat.

126
00:09:04,934 --> 00:09:07,056
Th-Then, does that mean we're officially a couple--

127
00:09:07,112 --> 00:09:08,767
No, it doesn't.

128
00:09:09,289 --> 00:09:11,378
Whaaaat?!

129
00:09:11,867 --> 00:09:14,578
I told you this evening, didn't I?

130
00:09:15,456 --> 00:09:17,389
"Will you marry me?"

131
00:09:32,184 --> 00:09:35,117
Akane-san?! What are you doing?!

132
00:09:35,217 --> 00:09:36,384
Urgh!?

133
00:09:36,430 --> 00:09:39,070
You should be more afraid of risks!

134
00:09:39,110 --> 00:09:42,897
Do you even realize how many people have died because of our carelessness?!

135
00:09:44,414 --> 00:09:48,094
You could have been killed too!

136
00:09:58,818 --> 00:10:00,752
Oh-hohohoho!

137
00:10:00,778 --> 00:10:04,338
Our company is going DX -- Deluxe, that is!

138
00:10:18,574 --> 00:10:21,467
An announcement from Astro Railway Corporation!

139
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:30,347
At last -- a service that lets you book every transit system in the entire solar system!

140
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,800
Its name--

141
00:10:37,334 --> 00:10:39,093
Mars.

142
00:10:50,585 --> 00:10:53,426
Do you have any idea how much damage

143
00:10:53,450 --> 00:10:56,278
the security incidents we've had before have caused?

144
00:10:56,465 --> 00:10:59,972
Incidents will happen. That's a certainty.

145
00:11:00,145 --> 00:11:03,918
Security measures, railway safety measures --

146
00:11:04,145 --> 00:11:07,732
they don't generate any direct economic benefit.

147
00:11:08,425 --> 00:11:11,798
But with proper preparation, we can reduce the damage.

148
00:11:12,545 --> 00:11:17,065
We need to invest in being ready for the worst-case scenario.

149
00:11:28,913 --> 00:11:33,547
Ahh...

150
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:37,980
Ahh...

151
00:11:38,413 --> 00:11:42,180
Ahhhh...
